P18-V01 Java batch decoder malformed-tail parity — 2026-10-22 20:53 UTC

Pinned source inspected: RocketMQ Java 5.5.1 commit
efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9. `MessageDecoder.decode` catches
record exceptions, advances the input buffer to its limit, and returns null;
`decodesBatch` stops at that null and returns its valid prefix. Production Rust
batch owners matching those Java call paths are pull result, POP reply, and two
admin query methods. One-record `view_message` remains separate.

Changed Rust to retain successful message prefixes in a new client-compatible
batch decoder while preserving strict `decode_many` errors. Wired pull, POP,
and both admin query owners to the compatible path. Pull processing reapplies
client IDs after compact expansion; this preserves inner `UNIQ_KEY` and
physical offset-ID behavior. Added a Java fixture with one valid record and a
malformed trailing byte, plus Common, pull, POP, and admin regressions.
Regenerated `fixtures/messages/records.json`; SHA-256:
d96af9e17c6a06adb1519eefcb66b546cea5c0e6bda52b3233a6b2fe5440ee6c.

Validation:
- Focused Common batch-prefix regression passed.
- Focused consumer pull and POP prefix regressions passed.
- Focused admin RPC prefix regression passed.
- `cargo test --offline --workspace --locked --quiet` passed.
- `cargo test --offline --workspace --all-features --locked --quiet` passed.
- `cargo clippy --offline --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed.
- `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed, including 37
  scenarios, 36 route/VIP cases, 106 typed headers, 19 typed bodies and 11
  message decode fixtures.

During validation, the first Maven verify detected the expected new-fixture
drift; regenerated the fixture with the existing `message-decode-fixtures`
entry point and reran the complete Maven gate successfully. The first full
workspace run also caught pull compact-expansion ID ordering; corrected ID
reattachment to preserve an existing subtype offset ID, then reran default and
all-feature workspace suites successfully. Code commit: `4e718e35`.

The batch malformed-tail slice is closed only. Broad P18-V01 reconciliation,
current-revision remote Ubuntu CI, native Windows runtime, and Phase 19
Broker/Docker evidence remain open. Protected Phase 19 working-tree paths were
